hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-18 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "After *mania*, mind at full intensity, *kin* is the next turn. *Kin* and *kind* come from the root for " (cons "to beget" (cons ", the same root as Latin *genus*, Greek *genos*, *gene*, *genius* and *engine*. To be kind is to treat someone as kin, as begotten of the same. *Genocide*, *genos* + *-cide*, is the killing of kind, which is to say of kin, which is to say of the begotten-together. The gene, the genius and the engine all come from the same begetting. An engineer was once an *ingeniator*, one with *ingenium*, inborn talent. Engineering the kernel and *genius* share the exact same root, and both share the root of the human kinship (*genos*) that genocide violates." nil)))) nil)
